I was never real fond of "tai broda" for "so [X]"  I understand it when
people use it that way, but I don't use it.  "mutce" seems to be much more
salient.  I think la'u works, though, too.  (What about ci'u?)  Or perhaps
"so" is really more of a noise word in these cases, so "iu" (or whatever)
is more appropriate?


  As for "dogs are so cute", I would prefer "loi" in that  construction (or
possibly even lo'e or le'e).  Man, doesn't anyone use anything but "lo"
anymore??

  So: "loi gerku cu .iu citmle"

            --gejyspa

